# Web-slinging changes what a spell costs, not when it may be cast (CR 702.188a, 601.3; ruling 2025-09-19: "You must
# follow all normal timing rules"). Bot1's Ornithopter attacks on turn 3 and is still tapped on Bot2's turn 4, with a
# Plains for {W}: Spider-Man, Web-Slinger, a creature without flash, is not offered for its web-slinging cost then. In
# Bot1's own main phase, with the Ornithopter tapped from attacking again, it is.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Ornithopter
Spider-Man, Web-Slinger
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
! Bot1.Hand.Spider-Man, Web-Slinger.Cast(Ability: Web-slinging)
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Hand.Spider-Man, Web-Slinger.Cast(Ability: Web-slinging)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
[T5 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Spider-Man, Web-Slinger
